  "note": "antic2: GTIA's colour-clock counter leads ANTIC's machine cycle by six clocks. emu states it as a constant -- GTIA_CC_ORIGIN = 6, cc = cyc*2 + h + 6 (system.c:216) -- and its comment names the test that pins the value: gtia_pmretrigger commits an HPOS write on scanline cycle 29 and needs the player already drawn at $40, so cc(29) must be 2*29 + 6 = 64. antic2 had no such origin: measured, its beam sits six colour clocks behind emu's at the same machine cycle. The fix is NOT to shift cc_pos -- the playfield source and the object comparison share the emit-window origin, so moving it would slide objects across the playfield and break four passing tests. It is a six-colour-clock delay on the HPOS registers as the object walk sees them: a position written during vertical blank is settled long before the beam arrives, so steady state is untouched, and only a mid-line write moves. gtia_pmoverlap is improved but not fixed -- it now clears three of twelve passes where it previously failed on the first position of the first.",
